     "text": "RECEIVED 14  -- ROI --\nCLINICAL SUMMARY - Powell LLC Clinic\n\nPatient: Lori Gordon DOB: 07/24/1993 Sex: F MRN: 338133\n\nEncounters:\n2026-06-03: The patient presented for a routine flu shot. Blood pressure was recorded at 150/88 mmHg, and weight was 169 pounds. The patient reported no significant complaints other than seeking the annual vaccination. The remainder of the physical examination was within normal limits, with no palpable lymphadenopathy, and the cardiac, respiratory, and examinations were unremarkable.\n\n2024-11-17: The patient visited for a follow-up concerning her history of breast cancer. Blood pressure at visit was 152/84 mmHg, and weight was 182 pounds. The patient is doing well with no evidence of recurrence. She remains off any systemic medications for her breast cancer, which is currently controlled. The patient's breast exams and mammograms are stable, with no new masses or suspicious findings. An ultrasound of the breasts was performed as a precautionary measure, which showed no abnormalities. We continue to rule out (r/o) a pulmonary nodule identified on a previous imaging study, pending follow-up imaging.\n\n2023-05-03: The patient presented with complaints of back strain. Blood pressure was 148/85 mmHg, and weight was 171 pounds. The patient reported lower back pain following a minor fall at home. On physical examination, there was tenderness in the lumbar region with no evidence of radiculopathy. X-rays of the lumbar spine were normal, and the patient was prescribed a short course of NSAIDs and physical therapy for symptomatic relief.\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n• Breast cancer, stage 0 (s/p treatment ~7 yrs ago) - controlled; meds: none\n - The patient's breast cancer, diagnosed as ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS), is currently controlled following treatment approximately seven years ago. There is no evidence of recurrence or metastasis, and the patient remains off any systemic therapies. Follow-up mammograms and ultrasounds have been consistently negative. Further imaging for a pulmonary nodule previously identified is pending. \n\n• Back strain \n - The patient's recent episode of back strain has resolved with conservative management, including NSAIDs and physical therapy. The patient is advised to avoid heavy lifting and to engage in exercises to strengthen the back muscles. \n\n• Rule out (r/o) pulmonary nodule\n - A small pulmonary nodule was noted on a previous imaging study, and we are currently monitoring this with follow-up imaging to ensure it remains stable and History:\n- Alcohol use: approximately 2 drinks per week"
